{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":413062,"duration_api_ms":474524,"num_turns":39,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"791861d3-e238-43c6-b313-c01f245df562","total_cost_usd":1.9128383999999994,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":78518,"cache_read_input_tokens":1433118,"output_tokens":11968,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":78518,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":11968,"cacheReadInputTokens":1433118,"cacheCreationInputTokens":78518,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.5066164999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":176,"outputTokens":12855,"cacheReadInputTokens":2469259,"cacheCreationInputTokens":75876,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.4062219000000002,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"amendments":[{"body":"In `affects_habitat_registry()` (actions.rs:159-169), `ChangePhotoperiod` is listed as affecting the habitat registry, but the habitat computation in `compute_habitat_registry` reads `hardware.light.intensity_index` not `hardware.light.photoperiod_hours`. Photoperiod changes produce a redundant registry refresh. Either remove `ChangePhotoperiod` from the match, or add a code comment explaining the deliberate over-approximation so future maintainers don't second-guess it.","rationale":"Minor correctness gap: the `affects_habitat_registry` predicate is documented as the canonical check for when the registry needs a refresh. Including a variant that has no habitat effect weakens that contract and introduces unnecessary computation. While harmless now, it could mask real oversights if maintainers trust the list as complete and exact."},{"body":"The legacy `total_colonizable_area_cm2()` (biology.rs:660-669) used by `algae_growth.rs:167` computes colonizable area as `wall_area_cm2 + substrate_layers.colonizable_area_cm2`, which omits `geometry.hardscape_area_cm2`. Now that hardscape area is a configurable field on `TankGeometry`, adding hardscape to a tank increases habitat registry `GlassHardscape` area but the algae carrying-capacity model ignores it entirely. Add a note (doc comment or inline TODO) clarifying this omission so the downstream habitatization task (tanksim-6e5.5.3) knows to migrate algae to the habitat registry rather than the legacy helper.","rationale":"The new `hardscape_area_cm2` field creates a silent divergence between the habitat registry and the only current consumer of colonizable area. A user could add 10,000 cm² of hardscape and see it reflected in the habitat snapshot but not in algae carrying capacity. A discoverable note prevents the discrepancy from becoming a latent surprise."}],"summary":"The habitat registry implementation is solid. `HabitatKind`, `HabitatEntry`, and `compute_habitat_registry` are well-structured with clear separation of derived state from source-of-truth fields. All exposure modifiers are correctly bounded [0,1] with both formula-level clamping and invariant enforcement. Colonizable areas are derived from geometry, hardware, substrate, and plant biomass as required. Save/load correctly treats the registry as derived state (always recomputed on load). Schema migrations v5→v6 and v6→v7 properly handle backward compatibility for the new fields. The test suite (32 tests) covers serialization roundtrips, area computation for all habitat kinds, modifier sensitivity to 7 distinct inputs, bounds under extreme scenarios, plant biomass responsiveness through the engine loop, and geometry scaling. All 400+ tests pass, clippy is clean. Two minor issues found: (1) `ChangePhotoperiod` unnecessarily triggers habitat refresh, and (2) the legacy `total_colonizable_area_cm2` used by algae growth now silently diverges from the habitat registry's GlassHardscape area when hardscape_area_cm2 is non-zero."},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0d5ae766-e65a-475e-a465-c8f58ef71d5f"}
